and exhibits intelligence and common knowledge consistent with that of a human child aged 2 (two). Testing has shown no unusual qualities to make it discernible from a non-sapient parsnip.</p> <p>Drawings are produced by SCP-5161-C but lack severely in quality as expected of a small child. Current drawings offer no conclusion to the origin of subject, language or other significant details.</p> <p>During the last years all three instances of SCP-5161 seem to have bonded together. It is currently unknown if all instances spark from the same origin, though this does seem to be unlikely since subjects were found in different countries and different years.</p> <p>By unknown anomalous means (suspected telepathy) are instances ‘able to communicate’ with each other. It is unknown what instances tell each other, if they even speak. It is not known how these instances communicate since they do not appear to speak each other languages.</p> <p><strong>Addendum SCP-5161-C</strong><br /> An unknown foundation personnel brought SCP-5161-C into containment, unknowingly, on 16-9-201█. During lunchbreak subject was experiencing increasing levels of trauma causing distress. Current theory is the subject startled in view of the knife, testing afterwards seems to cause the same effect but less dramatic when close to other SCP-5161 instances.</p> <p>Current SCP-5161 instances were known to have access to anomalous means, most notably telekinesis. The same effect is present in SCP-5161-C but far stronger especially observed during this event. Priorly unknown to the foundation the subject also able to put out a regional electro magnetic pulse blast (EMP) resulting in the containment breach of six (6) other SCP’s. This effect cost the lives of ██ foundation personnel while injuring ██ more.</p> <p>Camera’s and surveillance footage were unable to be reviewed as any live cameras were destroyed in the process of the episode. Due to unavailable footage it is currently not known who brought SCP-